<title>USA: Computer Sciences gets defense contract.</title>
<headline>Computer Sciences gets defense contract.</headline>
<dateline>FALLS CHURCH, Va. 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Computer Sciences Corp said on Friday that the U.S. Department of Defense has granted it a contract to provide infrastructure integration services at its various locations.</p>
<p>The indefinite delivery/indefinite quantity contract is valued at $285 million if all options are exercised during a five-year contract period, Computer Sciences said.</p>
<p>As the principal subcontractor, CSC's share on the contract could be valued at $72 million.</p>
</text>
